  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 205 PM EST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\n- Upper Low Moves East with Rain showers ending tonight\n\nLake effect rain showers will taper off overnight as the upper low\nmoves east followed by height rises and general subsidence for \nthe weekend with fair and cool weather through Sunday. A clipper \nwill move north of Lower Michigan on Sunday but deep moisture and \nprecip will remain north of the forecast area. Fair weather \ncontinues through the middle of the week in fast quasi-zonal flow.\n\n- Another Upper low and showers late week\n\nA northern stream shortwave trough tops the western CONUS upper\nridging and digs out a longwave trough across the eastern CONUS by\nThursday then merges with upper low over eastern Canada. The\nresulting height falls across the Great Lakes region will result\nin cooler temperatures with lake enhanced showers by the end of\nnext week.",
